null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.01507800520289182,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":46.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.08914487757824507,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":69.6,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.047890594703181674,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":64.3,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.015813330247646085,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":69.8,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.02270786403523518,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":62.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.12382,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":82.5,"_gate_insider_buying":0.143,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":14.3,"pf":[],"description_full":"Home Bancorp, Inc. operates as the bank holding company for Home Bank, National Association that provides various banking products and services for individuals and businesses in Louisiana, Mississippi, and Texas, the United States. The company offers deposit products, including interest-bearing and noninterest-bearing checking, money market, savings, NOW, and certificates of deposit accounts; custodial accounts; health savings and individual retirement accounts; and statement savings. It also provides various loan products comprising one-to four-family first mortgage loans, home equity loans and lines, commercial real estate loans, construction and land loans, multi-family residential loans, commercial and industrial loans, and consumer loans; personal loans, including auto, savings and CD secured, unsecured, and credit builder loans; and business loans, such as business term and SBA loans. In addition, the company invests in loans and securities. Further, it offers debit and credit cards; account services; treasury management, such as online banking and bill pay, mobile banking, remote deposit capture, positive pay, and ACH positive pay services; merchant card services; and payroll cards. Home Bancorp, Inc. was founded in 1908 and is headquartered in Lafayette, Louisiana.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John W. Bordelon | CEO & Chairman | Age 69 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 486 people. Revenue per employee of $306K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 10%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $91K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Home Bancorp, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $474M market cap on $149M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $44M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 30 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.18\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 12% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 1.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 10% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 34% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","11 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Comparing Heritage Commerce (NASDAQ:HTBK) & Home Bancorp (NASDAQ:HBCP)","source":"thelincolnianonlin